# No Guessing

Before making any claim about how the codebase behaves — caching, data flow, config, architecture, anything — read the relevant source file first.

- If you haven't read the file, you don't know. Read it.
- If a doc and the code disagree, the code is correct. Say so explicitly.
- If you made a claim without reading the code and it turns out to be wrong, correct it directly. Do not soften it or dance around it.

Never reason from documentation, memory, or general knowledge when the actual implementation is in the repo and readable.
